{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Who stretches out</b> — like <b>they stretched it out</b> (המה קרוהו)." "<b>His upper chambers</b> — they are the clouds, and they are in the sphere of the firmament." "And the meaning of <b>His riding</b> — to drive them." "And the meaning of <b>who walks</b> — on account of the decrees that descend through them, and He sends them to the places." "And the meaning of <b>wings of the wind</b> — in swift course."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:07.880464520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}